If a clinician continues an opioid-therapy for a patient and the patient has an overdose-history then the clinician should discuss an increased-overdose-risk with the patient and should weigh an opioid-benefit against a substantial-opioid-risk for the patient and should incorporate a risk-mitigation-strategy in a management-plan with the patient.
If a clinician continues an opioid-therapy for a patient and the patient has an overdose-history then the clinician may offer a naloxone-dose to the patient and may increase a patient-monitoring for the patient.
